Subject: [PATCH] PCC UDT MSS 1464 -> 1244 for a 1280-byte path MTU

ONLY apply this if the measurement path turns out to be the Tailscale overlay
(MTU 1280). Upstream src/wrappers/patches/pcc.patch already lowers UDT's MSS
from 1500 to 1464, i.e. 1500 minus the 36-byte pantheon-tunnel header. On a
1280-byte path the inner budget is 1280 - 36 = 1244, so 1464 overflows and the
datagrams fragment or are dropped.

This patch is NOT part of the default build: on a 1500-byte path it would make
PCC send needlessly small segments and the comparison with published numbers
would no longer hold. scripts/01_build_base.sh applies it only when
CCB_PATH_MTU=1280 is given.

--- a/sender/src/core.cpp
+++ b/sender/src/core.cpp
@@
-	m_iMSS = 1464;
+	m_iMSS = 1244;
--- a/receiver/src/core.cpp
+++ b/receiver/src/core.cpp
@@
-   m_iMSS = 1464;
+   m_iMSS = 1244;
--- a/sender/src/buffer.h
+++ b/sender/src/buffer.h
@@
-   CSndBuffer(const int& size = 64, const int& mss = 1464);
+   CSndBuffer(const int& size = 64, const int& mss = 1244);
--- a/receiver/src/buffer.h
+++ b/receiver/src/buffer.h
@@
-   CSndBuffer(int size = 32, int mss = 1464);
+   CSndBuffer(int size = 32, int mss = 1244);
